{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.ExplicitCentralIdempotent","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ExplicitCentralIdempotent","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Star.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Idempotents","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ExplicitCentralIdempotent.ExplicitCentralIdempotentConjecture.centralIdempotent_eq_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ExplicitCentralIdempotent.ExplicitCentralIdempotentConjecture.centralIdempotent_eq_sum","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ExplicitCentralIdempotent.lean#L116-L116","doc":"`e_λ` is the sum of the per-tableau projectors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ExplicitCentralIdempotent.ExplicitCentralIdempotentConjecture.proj_orth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ExplicitCentralIdempotent.ExplicitCentralIdempotentConjecture.proj_orth","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ExplicitCentralIdempotent.lean#L114-L114","doc":"Distinct tableaux carry distinct joint eigenvalue tuples, so their\nprojectors are orthogonal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ExplicitCentralIdempotent.ExplicitCentralIdempotentConjecture.proj_idem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ExplicitCentralIdempotent.ExplicitCentralIdempotentConjecture.proj_idem","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ExplicitCentralIdempotent.lean#L111-L111","doc":"Each projector is idempotent — Lagrange interpolation at a simple\njoint eigenvalue. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ExplicitCentralIdempotent.ExplicitCentralIdempotentConjecture.proj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ExplicitCentralIdempotent.ExplicitCentralIdempotentConjecture.proj","kind":"def","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ExplicitCentralIdempotent.lean#L108-L108","doc":"The Lagrange projector attached to one tableau. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ExplicitCentralIdempotent.ExplicitCentralIdempotentConjecture.fintypeTab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ExplicitCentralIdempotent.ExplicitCentralIdempotentConjecture.fintypeTab","kind":"def","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ExplicitCentralIdempotent.lean#L106-L106","doc":"Finitely many of them, so the decomposition is a finite sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ExplicitCentralIdempotent.ExplicitCentralIdempotentConjecture.Tab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ExplicitCentralIdempotent.ExplicitCentralIdempotentConjecture.Tab","kind":"def","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ExplicitCentralIdempotent.lean#L104-L104","doc":"The standard Young tableaux of shape `λ`, as an index type. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ExplicitCentralIdempotent.ExplicitCentralIdempotentConjecture.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ExplicitCentralIdempotent.ExplicitCentralIdempotentConjecture.mk","kind":"ctor","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ExplicitCentralIdempotent.lean#L102-L102","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ExplicitCentralIdempotent.ExplicitCentralIdempotentConjecture","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ExplicitCentralIdempotent.ExplicitCentralIdempotentConjecture","kind":"class","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ExplicitCentralIdempotent.lean#L77-L117","doc":"**CONJECTURE (OPEN)** — `conj:explicit-central-idempotent`.\n\nThe Murphy–Lagrange element `e_λ` decomposes as a sum, over the standard\nYoung tableaux of shape `λ`, of **pairwise-orthogonal idempotents** — the\nper-tableau Lagrange projectors\n\n    π_T = ∏_k ∏_{□ ≠ T(k)} (J_k - c(□;q)) / (c(T(k);q) - c(□;q))\n\nonto the joint `(c(T(1);q), …, c(T(n);q))`-eigenspace of the commuting\nJucys–Murphy elements.\n\n**This is the interpolation-theoretic INPUT, not the conclusion.** Earlier\nthis class had a single field whose type was\n`centralIdempotent lam q * centralIdempotent lam q = centralIdempotent lam q`\n— the downstream theorem's conclusion verbatim — and that theorem\ndischarged it by `exact hi.idempotent lam h`, a bare projection. AGENTS.md\n§3b-cond **item 5** forbids exactly that: a class must axiomatise the\nhypotheses and the theorem must *derive* its conclusion from them. Caught\n2026-09-04 by the `--item5` mode of\n`scripts/conditional-on-class-hypothesis-audit.ts`.\n\nThe three fields below are what Lagrange interpolation in commuting\nvariables actually supplies, and idempotency, orthogonality and\nsum-to-identity are all consequences of them rather than restatements.\n`explicit_central_idempotent_via_murphy` now composes them. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:explicit-central-idempotent","label":"conj:explicit-central-idempotent","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/conj-explicit-central-idempotent.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ExplicitCentralIdempotent.centralIdempotent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ExplicitCentralIdempotent.centralIdempotent","kind":"opaque","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ExplicitCentralIdempotent.lean#L64-L75","doc":"Murphy–Lagrange formula for the central primitive idempotent\n`e_λ ∈ Z(H_n(q))`. Placeholder element-of-the-algebra constant.\n\nPer Gemini PR #634 review: previous `: Type` signature was a\ntype-mismatch — `centralIdempotent` is an *element* of the\nalgebra carrier, not a type. The full Lean formalisation\nbinds it to `H.carrier` for an `IwahoriHeckeAlgebra` `H`; this\nplaceholder fixes the signature to return a value in the\nunderlying ring `R`, allowing element-level identities\n(orthogonality, self-adjointness, bar-pairing) to typecheck. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ExplicitCentralIdempotent.qContent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ExplicitCentralIdempotent.qContent","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ExplicitCentralIdempotent.lean#L44-L62","doc":"The q-content of a box at position `(i, j)` in a Young diagram:\n`c(i, j; q) = q^(2(j - i))`.\n\nThis is the integer (signed) power, so for boxes below the main\ndiagonal (`j < i`) the content is `q⁻²ᵏ` for some `k > 0`, i.e.\n`q ^ (n : ℤ)` must be total.\n\n§7c: that is supplied by carrying `q` as a **unit** `q : Rˣ` of a bare\n`CommRing R` — `Rˣ` is a group, so `zpow` is total there — rather than by\nstrengthening the base ring to a `GroupWithZero`/`Field`. The generic\nHecke ground ring `ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` is exactly this situation: `q` is a unit and\nthe ring is not a field.\n\nPer Gemini PR #634 review: previous `(2 * (j - i)).toNat` was\nmathematically incorrect — it forced `q^0 = 1` for all boxes\nbelow the diagonal, which contradicts the standard q-content\ndefinition (Hoefsmit, prop:hoefsmit-seminormal-form). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ExplicitCentralIdempotent.SYT","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ExplicitCentralIdempotent.SYT","kind":"opaque","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ExplicitCentralIdempotent.lean#L39-L42","doc":"A standard Young tableau of shape `λ`: a filling of the Young\ndiagram of `λ` with `1, ..., n` such that rows and columns\nincrease. Placeholder for Mathlib's eventual SYT API. ","signatureChunk":0}]}